-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",235,{
[7489]="70031BC3\n1\tFind your way into Fangorn and search for signs of life\tThe entrance to Fangorn can be found by following the edge of the trees and into a small clearing, where a light path can still be seen trailing into the forest. You should find a way into Fangorn and see what can be seen there.\n",
[7490]="70034A9B\n1\tTalk to Frethi\030Talk to Athelman\tCerdic has asked that you speak to his men to learn more of the Balewood before venturing into the forest.\n2\tStand at the nearby bunker and watch the road\tThe bunker can be found in Cerdic's camp overlooking the roadway to the east. You have spoken to Cerdic's men. You should now take up a post at the nearby bunker and watch the road for signs of Warg-riders.\n3\tTalk to Cerdic\tThe Orc raiding party has passed along the road. You should speak to Cerdic before venturing into the Balewood.\n",
[7491]="7004961C\n1\tEnter Naerband\tNaerband is located in Talath Úrui. You should enter Naerband.\n2\tSearch Naerband for information about Thraknûl\tNaerband is located in Talath Úrui. You should search Naerband for information about Thraknûl.\n3\tSearch Naerband for the guard\tThe guard abandoned the post. You should search Naerband's dungeons for the guard.\n4\tFind the lever that opens the torture chamber\tNaerband is located in Talath Úrui. You should find the lever that opens the torture chamber.\n5\tRetrieve the guard's key\tNaerband is located in Talath Úrui. You should retrieve the key from the corpse of the guard.\n6\tRetrieve and read the guard's register\tNaerband is located in Talath Úrui. You should retrieve and read the guard's register.\n7\tComplete Servants of Urudanî\030Complete The Key to Chaos\030Complete The Madness of Thraknûl\tNaerband is located in Talath Úrui. Now with the knowledge you have acquired through the guard's register, you should complete additional tasks within Naerband.\n8\tListen\tNaerband is located in Talath Úrui. You should listen.\n9\tListen more closely to the noise\tNaerband is located in Talath Úrui. You should listen more closely.\n10\tFind Akhrûn\tAkhrûn is in Naerband. You should find and speak with Akhrûn quickly.\n",
[7492]="7000E8B4\n1\tDefeat Hontimûrz\tNaerost lies to the east of Weathertop in the Lone-lands, far to the east of Bree. Nidgyl has asked you to assault the ruins of Naerost and defeat the villianous half-orc Hontimûrz. He suggested that you take allies with you.\n2\tTalk to Nidgyl\tNidgyl is in Bree-town in Bree-land, far to the west of Naerost. You should return to Nidgyl and tell him of Hontimûrz' defeat.\n",
[7493]="70042F2A\n1\tPatrol the entrance to the Morgul Vale\tThe Morgul Vale lies on the north-eastern border of South Ithilien. You should patrol the entrance to the Morgul Vale to see if the time is right to enter Osgiliath.\n2\tPatrol the cross-roads\tThe cross-roads lie on the northern border of South Ithilien. You should patrol the cross-roads.\n3\tPatrol the entrance to Osgiliath\tOsgiliath lies on the north-west border of South Ithilien. You should patrol the entrance of Osgiliath to see if the time is right to enter the ancient city.\n4\tReport back to Arodor\tFaramir's Look-out is located south-east of Osgiliath. You should speak with Arodor at Faramir's Look-out.\n5\tEnter Osgiliath through the south-eastern crack in the wall\tOsgiliath lies on the north-west border of South Ithilien. You should find the southern crack into Osgiliath.\n6\tEnter the culverts of Osgiliath\tThe culverts lie underneath the city of Osiliath. You should search for an entrance to the underground tunnels.\n7\tSearch for Rangers beneath Osgiliath\tThe culverts lie underneath the city of Osgiliath. You should search for a Ranger base in the tunnels under Osgiliath.\n",
[7494]="700642C3\n1\tTalk to Dolág\tRhúnelleth has suggested that you speak with Dolág, whose brother went missing while scouting the Poison Gardens of Carn Dûm. Dolág is at Bail Avarc, near Carn Dûm.\n2\tTalk to Dolág within Sant Lhoer, the Poison Gardens\tDetermined to rescue her missing brother, Dolág has asked you to meet her at the entrance of Sant Lhoer, the Poison Gardens. The Poison Gardens are located in Carn Dûm.\n3\tEnter Sant Lhoer and search for some sign of Málruv\tDolág has met you inside the gate of the Poison Gardens and is waiting for you to press on. You should look for her missing brother.\n4\tSearch the gazebo\tWhile exploring Sant Lhoer, you have come across a glass gazebo. You should search inside for signs of Málruv.\n5\tDefeat Cráthair\030Defeat Tarkka-oka\tWithin Sant Lhoer you have come across an Angmarim sorcerer, Cráthair, and his companion, the Jorthkyn Tarkka-oka. The latter is like nothing you have ever seen before. This must be one of Oganuin's foul experiments! You should defeat the pair.\n6\tTalk to Dolág\tWithin an iron and glass gazebo in Sant Lhoer, you were set upon by Tarkka-oka and his Keeper, Cráthair. Upon their defeat, you found an iron key. Dolág has joined you in the gazebo and is waiting to speak with you.\n7\tSearch for the north gate\tYou have discovered an iron key on the body of Cráthair. Dolág thinks it may unlock a gate she saw on the northern end of the Poison Gardens. You should search for and unlock the north gate.\n8\tContinue searching for Málruv\tYou leave the Poison Gardens behind and make your way towards enormous structures of iron and glass. You should continue searching for Málruv.\n9\tWait for, and then talk to, Dolág\tYou have discovered massive glass and iron greenhouses within Sant Lhoer. Wait for Dolág to catch up to you and then speak with her.\n10\tDefeat High Cultivator Oganuin\tYou stand before Bâr Heledh, the Glass House of Carn Dûm. Within its metal and glass walls the sorceress Oganuin practices her fell crafts, creating abominations and twisting living things towards unnatural ends. You must defeat her and search for signs of Málruv.\n11\tTalk to Málruv\tYou have found Málruv, and rescued him from the machinations of the Angmarim sorceress, Oganuin. You should speak with Málruv.\n12\tTalk to Dolág\tAfter defeating the sorceress Oganuin, you rescued Málruv and saw to his well-being. His worried sister is now waiting to speak with you. You should talk to Dolág\n13\tTalk to Dolág at Bail Avarc\tDolág waits to speak with you at Bail Avarc, near Carn Dûm.\n",
[7495]="70049566\n1\tTravel to the mouth of the abyss of Mordath in Dor Amarth\tThe abyss of Mordath can be found to the south-east of the Oath-taker's Horn in Dor Amarth. Spakorth has asked you to patrol the mouth of the abyss amidst the ruins of Barad-dûr, and search for any sign of King Váskmun Greytooth and the Firehorns.\n2\tTalk to Gimli at the abyss of Mordath\tGimli is standing near the mouth of the abyss of Mordath. You searched the mouth of the abyss, finding no sign of King Váskmun Greytooth or the Firehorns, but Gimli has now arrived at the Mordath. You should speak to him, and learn what he and Spakorth discovered.\n3\tTalk to Gimli at the abyss of Mordath\tGimli is standing near the mouth of the abyss of Mordath. You have learned that King Greytooth and the Firehorns have descended into the Abyss of Mordath. You should speak to Gimli and pursue them.\n4\tTalk to Spakorth at the ruins of Díngarth\tSpakorth can be found at the ruins of Díngarth in Dor Amarth. You and Gimli have escaped the ruins of Barad-dûr after confronting a glamour, and have returned to the ruins of Díngarth to tell Spakorth of what you discovered. You should speak to Spakorth.\n5\tTalk to Gimli at the ruins of Díngarth\tGimli can be found at the ruins of Díngarth. You have returned to the ruins of Díngarth from the dungeons of Barad-dûr after learning that King Váskmun Greytooth and the Firehorns have descended into the Mordath. Spakorth and his folk are free at long last, but the fate of Firehorns is still unwritten. You should speak to Gimli.\n",
[7496]="7000D4EA\n1\tDestroy the idol in Bail Dílas\030Destroy the idol in Bail Grundail\030Destroy the idol in Bail Cátharnakh\tThe idols of the Angmarim can be found in the three southern bails of Himbar, west of Gath Forthnír. Areneth has directed you into each of the three lower Bails in Himbar. At the centre of each Bail is an idol that must be destroyed to keep the Angmarim from ever attacking again.\n2\tTalk to Areneth\tAraneth is at Gath Forthnír, west of Himbar. Having destroyed the idols in Himbar, return to Gath Forthnír and tell Areneth what you have accomplished.\n",
[7497]="70035658\n1\tFind the owner of the camp-fire in Balewood\tThe camp-fire under the trees was spotted south-west from the Lonely Height. You should find the owners of the camp-fire, for they are probably refugees from Byre Tor.\n",
[7498]="7003E430\n1\tScout inside the troll-cave\tThe entrance to the troll-cave is north-east of Arrod's camp. You should scout inside the cave, as there are few trolls outside during the light of day.\n2\tScout inside the troll-cave\tThe entrance to the troll-cave is north-east of Arrod's camp. You should scout inside the cave, as there are few trolls outside during the light of day.\n3\tTalk to Arrod\tArrod is at his camp on the cliff south-west of the troll-cave. You should return to Arrod with tidings of your discovery in the troll-cave.\n",
[7499]="700544AF\n1\tMinas Morgul nestles among the mountains in Imlad Morgul. You should patrol the outer wall of the Dead City.\t\n2\tTalk to Damrod\tDamrod can be found at Echad Uial. You should talk to Damrod.\n3\tComplete 'Instance: Into the Circle of Wrath'\030Enter Barad Angarth, the Gate-wardens' Keep\tThe entrance to Barad Angarth can be found at the base of the outer wall of Minas Morgul. You should enter the tower of Barad Angarth.\n4\tTalk to Damrod in Barad Angarth\tDamrod can be found at Barad Angarth. You should talk to Damrod.\n",
[7500]="700272B1\n1\tCollect orders\tOne of the Dunlending captains might carry the orders Thurbald seeks. Thurbald has asked you to find a copy of the Draig-lûth's orders.\n2\tBring the orders to Thurbald\tThurbald is hiding to the south of Uvel-cadlus. You should bring the orders you found to Thurbald at once.\n",
[7501]="700529E9\n1\tTalk to Baradal\tBaradal is standing by in Arhaim. When you are ready to head into the wilds, you should speak to Baradal.\n2\tFollow the path west from Arhaim\tShathur-munzu is somewhere west of Arhaim. You should start by following the path west from the village.\n3\tTalk to Baradal\tYou have found a cart sitting by itself in the road. You should talk to Baradal about this.\n4\tFind the cart's owner\tBaradal believes the owner of the cart may still be alive somewhere in the forest west of Arhaim. You should search for the cart's owner.\n5\tTalk to Baradal\tBaradal can be called to your side with Baradal's summoning horn. You should talk to Baradal.\n6\tFind the missing horse\tThe dead cart owner's horse may still be alive somewhere in the forest of Duskenvale. You should find the missing horse.\n7\tFind the missing horse\tThe horse was spooked by your approach and ran deeper into the forest. You should find the missing horse again.\n8\tTalk to Baradal\tBaradal can be called to your side with Baradal's summoning horn. You should talk to Baradal about what just occurred.\n9\tFind Shathur-munzu\tShathur-munzu can be found west of Arhaim, in the wilds of Duskenvale. You should find Shathur-munzu.\n10\tTalk to Baradal\tBaradal can be called to your side with Baradal's summoning horn. You should talk to Baradal.\n",
[7502]="7002D7A6\n1\tCollect the sack of provisions near Oxi (quantity: see journal)\tOxi's sack of provisions lies on the ground beside him, in Jazârgund. Oxi has asked that you bring a sack of important provisions to the dwarf-outpost in the Fanged Pit.\n2\tTalk to Folkath in the Fanged Pit\tFolkath awaits the supplies at the camp in the Fanged Pit, at the end of the path east out of Jazârgund. Oxi has asked you to take the important provisions he has collected to Folkath in the Fanged Pit.\n",
[7503]="70042F70\n1\tSome people remain outside the keep, in the town of Arnach. You should gather the townsfolk outside the bailey walls and send them into the keep for their safety.\t\n2\tTalk to Indir\tIndir can be found within the walls of Arnach's keep. All the townsfolk of Arnach should now be gathered within the keep. You should return to Indir to tell him this has been done.\n",
[7504]="70058C8D\n1\tTalk to Órug\030Talk to Zhúdo\030Talk to Gárjan\tÓrug, Zhúdo, and Gárjan can be found in the trenches or on the battlefield in the War of Three Peaks. Glóin has sent you on a mission to join the forces of the Gabil'akkâ on the battlefield and receive reports from Órug, Zhúdo, and Gárjan before delivering his orders to Agnar Brokentooth at Ifbar-athrâkh.\n2\tAdvance to the forward trenches\tThe forward trenches can be found to the south of the ruins of Zudramdân in the War of Three Peaks. You have received reports from Órug, Zhúdo, and Gárjan. You should continue on to the forward trenches and deliver Glóin's orders to Agnar Brokentooth in Ifbar-athrâkh.\n3\tFind Agnar Brokentooth at Ifbar-athrâkh\tIfbar-athrâkh can be found beneath the hillside to the south-east of the forward trenches. You have arrived at the forward trenches and should now seek out Agnar Brokentooth in Ifbar-athrâkh.\n4\tDeliver Glóin's order to Agnar Brokentooth at Ifbar-athrâkh\tAgnar Brokentooth can be found at Ifbar-athrâkh. You have found Agnar Brokentooth in Ifbar-athrâkh. You should deliver Glóin's orders to Agnar Brokentooth at once.\n",
[7505]="7006BB24\n1\tTell Galâmka no\tTell Galâmka no, that you are not frightened and that you wish to help the people of Urash Dâr.\n2\tSpeak with Galâmka\tSpeak with Galâmka now that he knows you are not too scared to help.\n",
[7506]="7005304A\n1\tTalk to Radagast at Hultvís\tRadagast can be found at Hultvís. You should talk to Radagast.\n2\tTalk to Radagast at Hultvís\tRadagast can be found at Hultvís. You should talk to Radagast.\n3\tTalk to Varthmath at the Beorninghús\030Talk to Gandalf inside Grimbeorn's lodge\tVarthmath and Gandalf can be found at the Beorninghús. You should talk to Varthmath and Gandalf.\n4\tTravel to the Gladden Fields with Gandalf to meet with Radagast\tRadagast can be found on the northern edge of the Gladden Fields. You should travel to the Gladden Fields to meet with Radagast and Gandalf.\n5\tTalk to Radagast in the Gladden Fields\tRadagast can be found on the northern edge of the Gladden Fields. You should talk to Radagast in the Gladden Fields.\n6\tTalk to Gandalf in the Gladden Fields\tGandalf can be found on the northern edge of the Gladden Fields. You should talk to Gandalf in the Gladden Fields.\n7\tTalk to Varthmath in the Gladdenmere\tVarthmath can be found at the old dock in the south-east side of the Gladdenmere. You should talk to Varthmath in the Gladdenmere.\n",
[7507]="70008766\n1\tScout the Grimwood Lumber-yard\tThe Grimwood Lumber-yard is found in the heart of the Grimwood within Hithlad, south and east across the Hoardale River. Soldier Faltúrz ordered you to learn the location of the Grimwood Lumber-yard.\n2\tReturn to Soldier Faltúrz at Gramsfoot\tSoldier Faltúrz awaits your return at the Krahjarn-encampment at Gramsfoot. You scouted through the Grimwood and discovered the Grimwood Lumber-yard. Now you should return to Soldier Faltúrz.\n",
[7508]="70061383\n1\tDefeat the Heirs of Thyrstáth\030Enter Abnankâra\tFollowing the death of their chieftain, Hrungrod, at the hands of the dwarves, the heirs of Thyrstáth have pledged themselves into the service of Hrímil Frost-heart.\n2\tDefeat Thrall-lord Dushtalbúk\tFallen under the sway of Hrímil Frost-heart's voice, Thrall-lord Dushtalbúk leads the Orcs of Gundabad in defending the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra.\n3\tDefeat Hrímil Frost-heart\tAfter suffering an unexpected defeat atop Mount Gundabad, Hrímil Frost-heart, the Herald of Winter, retreated to the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra to tend her wounds and prepare for the final confrontation with Durin.\n4\tCompleted: Into the Hiddenhoard (Tier 1)\tYou have completed the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra on Tier 1.\n",
[7509]="70061391\n1\tDefeat the Heirs of Thyrstáth\030Enter Abnankâra\tFollowing the death of their chieftain, Hrungrod, at the hands of the dwarves, the heirs of Thyrstáth have pledged themselves into the service of Hrímil Frost-heart.\n2\tDefeat Thrall-lord Dushtalbúk\tFallen under the sway of Hrímil Frost-heart's voice, Thrall-lord Dushtalbúk leads the Orcs of Gundabad in defending the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra.\n3\tDefeat Hrímil Frost-heart\tAfter suffering an unexpected defeat atop Mount Gundabad, Hrímil Frost-heart, the Herald of Winter, retreated to the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra to tend her wounds and prepare for the final confrontation with Durin.\n4\tCompleted: Into the Hiddenhoard (Tier 2)\tYou have completed the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra on Tier 2.\n",
[7510]="70061396\n1\tDefeat the Heirs of Thyrstáth\030Enter Abnankâra\tFollowing the death of their chieftain, Hrungrod, at the hands of the dwarves, the heirs of Thyrstáth have pledged themselves into the service of Hrímil Frost-heart.\n2\tDefeat Thrall-lord Dushtalbúk\tFallen under the sway of Hrímil Frost-heart's voice, Thrall-lord Dushtalbúk leads the Orcs of Gundabad in defending the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra.\n3\tDefeat Hrímil Frost-heart\tAfter suffering an unexpected defeat atop Mount Gundabad, Hrímil Frost-heart, the Herald of Winter, retreated to the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra to tend her wounds and prepare for the final confrontation with Durin.\n4\tCompleted: Into the Hiddenhoard (Tier 3)\tYou have completed the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra on Tier 3.\n",
[7511]="70061397\n1\tDefeat the Heirs of Thyrstáth\030Enter Abnankâra\tFollowing the death of their chieftain, Hrungrod, at the hands of the dwarves, the heirs of Thyrstáth have pledged themselves into the service of Hrímil Frost-heart.\n2\tDefeat Thrall-lord Dushtalbúk\tFallen under the sway of Hrímil Frost-heart's voice, Thrall-lord Dushtalbúk leads the Orcs of Gundabad in defending the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra.\n3\tDefeat Hrímil Frost-heart\tAfter suffering an unexpected defeat atop Mount Gundabad, Hrímil Frost-heart, the Herald of Winter, retreated to the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra to tend her wounds and prepare for the final confrontation with Durin.\n4\tCompleted: Into the Hiddenhoard (Tier 4)\tYou have completed the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra on Tier 4.\n",
[7512]="70061398\n1\tDefeat the Heirs of Thyrstáth\030Enter Abnankâra\tFollowing the death of their chieftain, Hrungrod, at the hands of the dwarves, the heirs of Thyrstáth have pledged themselves into the service of Hrímil Frost-heart.\n2\tDefeat Thrall-lord Dushtalbúk\tFallen under the sway of Hrímil Frost-heart's voice, Thrall-lord Dushtalbúk leads the Orcs of Gundabad in defending the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra.\n3\tDefeat Hrímil Frost-heart\tAfter suffering an unexpected defeat atop Mount Gundabad, Hrímil Frost-heart, the Herald of Winter, retreated to the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra to tend her wounds and prepare for the final confrontation with Durin.\n4\tCompleted: Into the Hiddenhoard (Tier 5)\tYou have completed the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra on Tier 5.\n",
[7513]="7000C767\n1\tTalk to Eywind in the High Pass\tFind Eywind and his companions in the High Pass, through the passage that runs past Pinnath Fenui and through Cirith Daur to the east.\n",
[7514]="7004E75A\n1\tTalk to Spall\tSpall can be found before Thorin's throne in the court of Erebor. You should hear Spall's reply to King Thorin Stonehelm.\n2\tTalk to King Thorin\tThorin stands before his throne in the court of Erebor. You should hear King Thorin's Stonehelm reply.\n3\tMeet Spall in the Ironfold\tYou should meet Spall the Lore-master in the Ironfold, which lies down the road that leads from the south-eastern gates of Dale.\n4\tInvestigate Skald's Drop\030Investigate Utterby\030Investigate Járnfast's foundations\030Investigate the Dwarves of Járnfast\tSkald's Drop lies along the southern edge of the Ironfold, Utterby right in the middle, and Járnfast at its eastern edge. You should investigate the rumours about the Iron Hills near the stair at Skald's Drop, in the Dalish town of Utterby, and at the keep of Járnfast where Lord Náin dwells. If you get separated from Spall, use the horn to call him back.\n5\tTalk to Spall\tYou should talk to Spall the Lore-master.\n6\tTalk to Lord Náin again\tYou should talk to Lord Náin again, at his seat in Járnfast in the Iron Hills.\n",
[7515]="7004E7C5\n1\tYou should talk to the Dwarves of Járnfast, including Lord Náin.\t\n2\tTalk to Spall\tNow that you have talked to many dwarves in Járnfast, you should talk once more to Spall.\n",
[7516]="7004E75B\n1\tInvestigate the foundations of Járnfast\tInvestigate the rumours about the structural integrity of Járnfast.\n2\tTalk to Spall\tYou should talk to Spall about the foundations of Járnfast.\n3\tInspect cracks around Járnfast (total: 15)\tYou should examine cracks in the stonework of Járnfast, both inside and out.\n4\tTalk to Spall\tNow that you have inspected a great number of the cracks apparent in Járnfast's stonework, you should talk to Spall.\n",
[7517]="7004E759\n1\tInvestigate Skald's Drop\tInvestigate the rumours about Skald's Drop and the Stair with Spall.\n2\tTalk to Spall\tYou should talk to Spall about the rumours regarding Skald's Drop.\n3\tFind the Stair\tYou should view the Stair in the cliff's edge, at Skald's Drop in the Ironfold.\n4\tTalk to Spall\tYou should talk to Spall, now that you have seen the Stair at Skald's Drop.\n5\tInvestigate the small camp\tYou should look for a camp-fire inland near Skald's Drop, and see if there are any of the rumoured travellers there.\n6\tTalk to the strange dwarves\tYou should talk to the strange dwarves you found at a camp-fire near to Skald's Drop in the Ironfold.\n7\tCollect small sacks (total: 8)\030Collect larger parcels (total: 4)\030Collect water-skins (total: 4)\tThe possessions are scattered near to Skald's Drop in the Ironfold. You should help the strange dwarves gather their scattered possessions, including small sacks, big parcels, and water-skins.\n8\tReturn to Okuz and Túmo\tYou should bring the belongings you gathered to Okuz and Túmo at their camp, near Skald's Drop.\n9\tFind the axe\tYou should search for Okuz and Túmo's axe, which they say 'ran' off away from their camp near Skald's Drop, toward the river.\n10\tBring the axe to Okuz and Túmo\tYou should return the axe to the strange dwarves at their camp-site near Skald's Drop. You should also ask them why the axe was tied to an ox.\n11\tTalk to Spall\tYou should hear what Spall has to say in response to Okuz's claims.\n12\tTalk to Okuz\tOkuz and Túmo stand by their camp-fire, near Skald's Drop in the Ironfold. Hear Okuz's answer to Spall's charge.\n13\tTalk to Spall\tYou should talk to Spall and hear his thoughts on what you have found in the Ironfold.\n",
[7518]="7004E75C\n1\tInvestigate Utterby\tInvestigate the rumours about the Dalish town of Utterby.\n2\tTalk to Spall\tYou should talk to Spall about investigating the rumours regarding Utterby.\n3\tView Utterby's south gate\030View Utterby's east gate\030Learn who controls Utterby now\030Find signs of what happened\tYou should scout Utterby with Spall, making sure to get a view of the south and east gates, and looking out for signs of who controls the town now and how that came to pass.\n4\tTalk to Spall\tNow that you have scouted the perimeter of Utterby, you should talk to Spall.\n",
[7519]="70071623\n1\tTalk to Ishûri\tArâniz believes you will need the escaped thralls' help to get into Esh Mêkag. You should talk to Ishûri and mention the name 'Ebuzâm'.\n2\tTalk to Ishûri to enter Esh Mêkag\tIshûri has agreed to show you the secret way into Esh Mêkag. You should talk to Ishûri when you are ready to enter Esh Mêkag.\n3\tTalk to Ishûri\tYou have entered Esh Mêkag via the escapees' secret route. You should talk to Ishûri in Esh Mêkag. If you need to re-enter Esh Mêkag, talk to Ishûri in Dur Nâgu.\n4\tFind Ebuzâm\tYou should find Ebuzâm somewhere in the Esh Mêkag pit-mine. If you need to re-enter Esh Mêkag, talk to Ishûri in Dur Nâgu.\n5\tFree Enûtu\030Free Shakûl\030Free the kidnapped Beltáni\030Free the captive Aradûni\tYou must help some prisoners escape Esh Mêkag before Ebuzâm will leave. You should rescue Ebuzâm's children, Enûtu and Shakûl, as well as the Aradûni soldiers and the kidnapped Beltáni. If you need to re-enter Esh Mêkag, talk to Ishûri in Dur Nâgu.\n6\tUse the tunnel to return to Dur Nâgu\tYou have rescued who you can. You should return to Dur Nâgu using the secret tunnel.\n7\tTalk to Arâniz\tYou have successfully rescued many prisoners from Esh Mêkag. You should report your success to Arâniz in Dur Nâgu.\n",
[7520]="700431B3\n1\tComplete 'Volume II, Book 1: The Walls of Moria' by speaking to Ráthwald near Echad Dúnann and completing his quest chain\tSpalvi has agreed to meet you just inside the entrance to the dwarf-kingdom of Moria once the Iron Garrison has opened the Doors of Durin at the Hollin Gate.\n2\tTalk to Spalvi in Durin's Threshold, in the Great Delving of Moria\tSpalvi Stout-heart is in Durin's Threshold, just inside the western entrance to Moria. Spalvi has decided that following the Iron Garrison into Moria is your best hope of finding Bingo Boffin.\n3\tTalk to Ketill Map-maker at the Dolven-view, in the Great Delving\tKetill Map-maker is in the Dolven-view, located in the Great Delving of Moria. Spalvi has heard that a dwarf with the Iron Garrison named Ketill is making maps of Khazad-dûm and might be able to help you find Bingo.\n4\tKetill Map-maker has asked you to fight enemies in Gazatmur, east of the Dolven-view, until he is done working.\t\n5\tTalk to Ketill Map-maker overlooking Gazatmur, east of the Dolven-view\tKetill Map-maker can be found perched on a wall overlooking Gazatmur, east of the Dolven-view.\n6\tKetill Map-maker has asked you to fight enemies in Katûb-zahar, north-east of the Dolven-view, until he is done working.\t\n7\tTalk to Ketill Map-maker on the highest ledge of Katûb-zahar\tKetill Map-maker can be found on the highest ledge in the middle of the library of Katûb-zahar, north-east of the Dolven-view.\n8\tTalk to Spalvi at the Dolven-view, in the Great Delving\tSpalvi is in the Dolven-view, in the Great Delving of Moria.\n",
})
